text:
rachel: quick thread — trying to nail focus-recovery + breadcrumb semantics for deep links that open micro-views (tabs/anchors) from shared URLs. want to avoid janky scroll/focus jumps and keep breadcrumbs meaningful. thoughts?

tom: short q: when a link opens a subview, do we want the breadcrumb to encode the subview (e.g. /Console / Models / X / Metrics) or leave crumbs as the resource only and surface the subview in the header? both have tradeoffs for copy/share.

li: prefer encoding the subview in breadcrumbs. it makes the link state discoverable and clickable to collapse back. clicking the crumb should close the subview and restore prior focus.

anjali: accessibility note: programmatic focus must always be accompanied by an announcement, e.g., `aria-live="polite"` message like "Metrics panel opened" or using `role=region aria-labelledby`. screen reader users need that context.

rachel: agreed. also we need a predictable focus-return when the subview is closed (ESC, crumb click, or back). store the origin element id before moving focus, then restore it on close. if origin not found, fall back to the main heading.

focus-bot: automated suggestion: add util `captureOrigin(el)` + `restoreOrigin()`; include fallback logic and an opt-out if the opener was via keyboard vs mouse so we can choose whether to focus the opener or the next logical item.

li: history behavior: initial deep-link should use `replaceState` so the back button doesn't immediately close the whole page. but if user navigates inside the subview (e.g., opens a nested tab), we `pushState`. keep these rules consistent.

anjali: another a11y nit: when we focus a heading with `element.focus()` some browsers won't visibly show the focus ring. we should add a helper class like `.js-focused` applied briefly to ensure focus-visible styling. also respect `:focus-visible` when available.

rachel: perf point: many dashboards render lots of widgets. if the URL contains `?panel=metrics#p95`, hydrate the metrics panel first, not the whole page. show skeleton and `aria-busy=true` while waiting for data. only scroll/focus after the target exists.

li: code sketch for deferred focus: ```js
// pseudo
captureOrigin();
await waitForResource(id);
mountPanel('metrics');
const target = document.getElementById('p95');
if (target) {
  target.setAttribute('tabindex','-1');
  target.focus({preventScroll:true});
  target.scrollIntoView({behavior:'auto', block:'center'});
  target.removeAttribute('tabindex');
}
```

tom: breadcrumb UX: render an extra crumb for the panel. crumb click should call our `closePanel()` which restores focus and calls `history.replaceState` to remove `panel=`. also make crumb accessible: a11y label `Close metrics panel` when focused.

anjali: highlight for shared links: if `?highlight=p95` show an ARIA-visible hint `aria-describedby='shared-hint'` and a non-animated high-contrast box for reduced-motion users. pulse animation only if `prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference`. ensure color contrast passes WCAG.

focus-bot: route-scan: identical deep-link shape detected in `/console/datasets/*` and `/console/projects/*`. recommend extracting a central `applyDeepPanel` handler to normalize lifecycle: parse -> fetch -> mount -> focus -> analytics.

rachel: analytics: fire `nav.panel_opened` with {path, panel, anchor, via_deeplink:true, opened_via: 'link'|'in-app'}. track focus restore success boolean for regressions.

li: tests: unit tests for URL normalization (strip trailing slash, lowercase id), e2e for keyboard-only flow (open via link, focus lands in panel, ESC returns focus), SR regression test (announce message present).

anjali: QA checklist: screen reader narration, focus-visible after JS focus, skip links unaffected, color-contrast on shared highlight, keyboard return semantics.

rachel: UX question: auto-expand leftnav groups when deep link arrives vs highlight only? for discoverability I lean auto-expand, but only session-scoped (don’t write to profile prefs).

tom: auto-expand but ephemeral makes sense. make sure DOM order places the target link before focusing. otherwise SR users might not reach it via linear navigation.

li: one more edge: if resource id is invalid/stale, show a friendly inline message and do not attempt focus/scroll. analytics should record `nav.panel_open_failed` with reason.

rachel: thanks all — i'll author the pattern doc with: canonical URL examples, focus capture/restore utils, deferred-open sketch, history rules, analytics schema, and the a11y QA checklist. planning to open a PR later today; pls review then. :sparkles:
